   "sentenceId": 8,
   "he": "״וּבֶעָשׂוֹר שֶׁבְּחוֹמֶשׁ הַפְּקוּדִים קוֹרֵא עַל פֶּה״. וְלִיכְרְכֵיהּ לְסֵפֶר וְלִיקְרֵי! אָמַר רַב הוּנָא בַּר יְהוּדָה אָמַר רַב שֵׁשֶׁת: לְפִי שֶׁאֵין גּוֹלְלִין סֵפֶר תּוֹרָה בַּצִּבּוּר.",
   "en": "It is stated in the mishna that «he reads by heart» the portion beginning with: «“And on the tenth,” from the book of Numbers» (29:7–11). The Gemara asks: «But let him furl the» Torah «scroll» to that portion «and read» it from the text. «Rav Huna bar Yehuda says» that «Rav Sheshet says:» This is not done «because one may not furl a Torah scroll in public,» out of respect for the congregation."
  }
